# Line endings: LF everywhere, no exceptions.
#
# This repo's payload is shell scripts, Python scripts and a systemd unit
# that execute on Raspberry Pi OS. A CRLF shebang is not a valid
# interpreter path -- `#!/bin/sh\r` fails at exec time with
#
#     bad interpreter: No such file or directory
#
# which is a confusing error, since the file plainly exists. The systemd
# unit fails the same way on its ExecStart. Editing on Windows without
# this file silently rewrites every file to CRLF; committing that would
# break the repo for every user, including via the `curl | bash`
# one-liner in README.md.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` means: detect text vs binary, store text as LF in
# the repository, and check it out as LF on every platform -- Windows
# included. Editors handle LF fine; Notepad has since Win10 1809.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit for the executable payload, so intent survives someone
# relaxing the wildcard above.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
